  "full_text": "I made a bridge design game. This one is inside Sparrow OS. There's another one that's called SimStructure that's a Windows application. Anyway, I made that in 2001. You can download SimStructure from my website, from the Sparrow OS website. This is part of Sparrow. I'm connecting with concrete. Concrete is good in compression and bad in tension. That means when you pull it apart, it crumbles easily. The goal is to design a cheap bridge. I think on this one, it doesn't have a... You make up your own rules. I'm going to test it. Okay, it broke. Now, let's see. Let's put some... Let's put steel. Oops. Actually, I could have just done wire. Let's do wire. This is a slightly tensioned wire. I don't know if this is going to help any... Crazy design. Anyway, uh... It's breaking. It's breaking. Anyway, so, uh... Uh... Have fun. Uh... Uh... Uh... Uh... Uh... Uh... Uh... Thank you.",
